---
import PublicLayout from "@/layouts/PublicLayout.astro";
import { Card, CardContent } from "@/components/ui/card";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, SITE_OPERATOR } from "@/lib/site";

// Every statement below must stay true for the code as it is: a change to the data model, to who sees what, to
// deletion, to the cookies or to the providers updates this page in the same change (CLAUDE.md, Conventions).
const contactHref = `mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`;
// Kept in one expression so the name the smoke test pins can never be split by reformatting.
const SUPERVISORY_AUTHORITY = "Prezes Urzędu Ochrony Danych Osobowych";
const h2 = "font-heading mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-foreground";
const p = "mt-3 leading-relaxed";
const ul = "mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 leading-relaxed";
const link = "font-medium text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline";
---

<PublicLayout title="Privacy Policy">
  <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 sm:py-14">
    <Card>
      <CardContent className="text-base text-muted-foreground">
        <h1 class="font-heading text-3xl font-semibold text-foreground">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm">
          Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-08">8 October 2026</time>
        </p>
        <p class:list={p}>
          This page explains what StreakBoard collects about you, why, who can see it, how long it is kept and what you
          can ask us to do with it.
        </p>

        <section>
          <h2 class:list={h2}>Who we are</h2>
          <ul class:list={ul}>
            <li>
              StreakBoard is run by {SITE_OPERATOR}, a private individual, who is the controller of your personal data.
            </li>
            <li>
              Contact:{" "}
              <a href={contactHref} class:list={link}>
                {CONTACT_EMAIL}
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>There is no data protection officer.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class:list={h2}>What we collect</h2>
          <ul class:list={ul}>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-foreground">Your account:</strong> your e-mail address, a hash of your password kept
              by our sign-in provider, Supabase Auth (the app itself never stores your password), and when you signed up
              and last signed in.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-foreground">With "Continue with Google":</strong> the name, e-mail address and profile
              picture that Google shares. The app uses only the e-mail address.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-foreground">Your sessions:</strong> for each signed-in session, the IP address and the
              browser you use (user agent), plus a security log of account events (such as sign-ins) with the IP
              address, kept by Supabase Auth.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-foreground">What you create:</strong> your group's name, task titles (free text, so
              please keep anything sensitive out of them), memberships, the tasks you join and the days or weeks you
              mark done.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-foreground">Technical data:</strong>
              <ul class:list={ul}>
                <li>our own log entries: the route, your user id, a request id and the time;</li>
                <li>
                  error reports, which identify you only by your user id and never contain cookies, headers, request
                  bodies or query strings;
                </li>
                <li>our own log entries and error reports mask e-mail addresses and invite codes;</li>
                <li>
                  Cloudflare, which hosts the site, processes your IP address and request details to serve it, and its
                  request logs record each address you request (an invite link contains its code) with request details
                  such as your IP address.
                </li>
              </ul>
            </li>
            <li>No analytics, no advertising and no tracking scripts.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class:list={h2}>Why we use it and on what legal basis</h2>
          <ul class:list={ul}>
            <li>
              To run your account and the group features (creating and joining a group, tasks, marking them done,
              streaks and the leaderboard) and to send the sign-up confirmation e-mail: performance of the contract,
              which is your use of StreakBoard (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR).
            </li>
            <li>
              To keep the service secure and to find and fix errors (request logs, error reports, session data and the
              security log): our legitimate interest in a working and secure service (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class:list={h2}>Who can see your data</h2>
          <ul class:list={ul}>
            <li>
              The other members of your group see your e-mail address, the tasks you create and join, the days or weeks
              you mark done, your streaks and your place on the leaderboard.
            </li>
            <li>Anyone signed in who has your group's invite link can see the group's name before joining.</li>
            <li>
              When you leave a group, or its owner removes you, your participation and the days or weeks you marked done
              in its tasks are deleted and the group no longer shows your e-mail address. Tasks you created stay in the
              group.
            </li>
            <li>Nobody else sees your e-mail address in the app.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class:list={h2}>Service providers and transfers</h2>
          <ul class:list={ul}>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-foreground">Cloudflare:</strong> hosting, the domain, DNS and request logs.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-foreground">Supabase:</strong> the database and sign-in. The database is in the EU
              (Ireland); the contracting party is Supabase Pte. Ltd. (Singapore), under Standard Contractual Clauses.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-foreground">Resend:</strong> sends the confirmation e-mail and keeps account data,
              e-mail metadata and logs in the United States.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-foreground">Sentry:</strong> error reports; it may process data in the United States.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-foreground">Google:</strong> acts under its own terms when you choose "Continue with
              Google".
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class:list={p}>
            Transfers outside the European Economic Area rely on the EU–US Data Privacy Framework and/or Standard
            Contractual Clauses.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class:list={h2}>How long we keep it</h2>
          <ul class:list={ul}>
            <li>Your account, what you create, session data and the security log: until your account is deleted.</li>
            <li>Request logs, ours and Cloudflare's: up to 7 days.</li>
            <li>
              Error reports: up to 90 days (30 days on Sentry's free plan, 90 days while an organization trial runs).
            </li>
            <li>E-mail delivery logs: 30 days.</li>
            <li>Supabase platform logs: 1 day.</li>
            <li>Cookies: see the next section.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class:list={h2}>Cookies</h2>
          <p class:list={p}>StreakBoard sets only strictly necessary cookies:</p>
          <ul class:list={ul}>
            <li>
              the session cookie (<code>sb-…-auth-token</code>, possibly split into numbered parts) keeps you signed in;
              it is removed when you sign out and otherwise lasts up to 400 days after it was last refreshed;
            </li>
            <li>
              a sign-in check cookie (<code>sb-…-code-verifier</code>) is used during e-mail sign-up and Google sign-in;
            </li>
            <li>
              <code>join_code</code> (1 hour) remembers an invite while you sign in;
            </li>
            <li>
              <code>auth_email</code> (60 seconds) refills the e-mail field after a failed attempt.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class:list={p}>
            We do not ask for consent, because none of these cookies is used for anything but the service you asked for.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class:list={h2}>Your rights</h2>
          <p class:list={p}>
            You have the right to access your data, to have it corrected or erased, to restrict its processing and to
            receive it in a portable form.
          </p>
          <p class:list={p}>
            <strong class="text-foreground">Right to object.</strong> You have the right to object at any time to the
            processing of your data based on our legitimate interests (Art. 21 GDPR).
          </p>
          <p class:list={p}>
            To use any of these rights, write to{" "}
            <a href={contactHref} class:list={link}>
              {CONTACT_EMAIL}
            </a>{" "}
            and you get an answer within one month.
          </p>
          <p class:list={p}>
            You can also complain to the Polish supervisory authority, the {SUPERVISORY_AUTHORITY}, ul. Stawki 2, 00-193
            Warszawa, by post or through the{" "}
            <a href="https://uodo.gov.pl" class:list={link}>
              uodo.gov.pl
            </a>{" "}
            website.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class:list={h2}>Deleting your account</h2>
          <ul class:list={ul}>
            <li>
              There is no delete button yet. Write to{" "}
              <a href={contactHref} class:list={link}>
                {CONTACT_EMAIL}
              </a>{" "}
              from your account's e-mail address, and your account and the data kept until deletion (see "How long we
              keep it") are deleted within one month.
            </li>
            <li>
              If you own a group, the group is deleted with all its tasks and every member's participation and the days
              or weeks they marked done in it; the other members keep their accounts.
            </li>
            <li>
              Tasks you created in someone else's group are deleted together with the other members' participation and
              the days or weeks they marked done on them.
            </li>
            <li>Leaving a group keeps your account.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class:list={h2}>Do you have to give us your data</h2>
          <ul class:list={ul}>
            <li>An e-mail address is needed to create an account; without it the service cannot work.</li>
            <li>
              There are no automated decisions with legal or similarly significant effects; the leaderboard only adds up
              streaks.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class:list={h2}>Changes</h2>
          <p class:list={p}>Changes to this policy are published on this page with a new date.</p>
        </section>
      </CardContent>
    </Card>
  </div>
</PublicLayout>
